{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator-authorized default 2026-09-07: use per-process/per-session unique scratch/log paths (e.g. mktemp/tempfile-managed directory or a PID+session-id suffix) instead of fixed shared `/tmp/<name>` files. Rationale: unique paths are the universal concurrency-safe default for evidence artifacts; fixed names allow overlapping sessions to silently overwrite or interleave each other's logs."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788785850902276142,"uuid":"8ccb67a6-2f58-40c3-83c8-d002fc34c63e"}